    "question": {
      ":question/id": "686975ba-7ad1-561c-97ec-77cdaafe7f8a",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=e^{x} - 2$\n- **II.** $y=- e^{x} - 2$\n- **III.** $y=- 3 e^{x} - 2$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=e^{x} - 2,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=e^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}1\\cdot \\left(e^{x} - 2\\right) \\\\ e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}e^{x} - 2 \\\\ 2 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=e^{x} - 2$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=- e^{x} - 2,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- e^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ - e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}1\\cdot \\left(- e^{x} - 2\\right) \\\\ - e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}- e^{x} - 2 \\\\ 2 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=- e^{x} - 2$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=- 3 e^{x} - 2,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 3 e^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ - 3 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}1\\cdot \\left(- 3 e^{x} - 2\\right) \\\\ - 3 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}- 3 e^{x} - 2 \\\\ 2 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=- 3 e^{x} - 2$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"",
